  "text": "## Your first Siargao trip (4 days, mid budget)\n\nBase yourself in General Luna near Cloud 9. You get surf, island hopping and Sugba Lagoon without long transfers.\n\n**Day 1: Land and settle in General Luna**\n- 10:30: Land at Sayak Airport (IAO), Del Carmen (Direct flights from Manila, Cebu and Clark)\n- 11:15: Shared van to General Luna (About 1 hour, around PHP 350 per person)\n- 14:00: Check in near Cloud 9\n- 17:30: Sunset on the Cloud 9 boardwalk\n- 19:30: Dinner on Tourism Road\n\n**Day 2: Surf lesson and the Maasin river**\n- 07:00: Beginner surf lesson at Jacking Horse (About PHP 1,500 for 1.5 hours with board and coach)\n- 12:00: Lunch and a nap, it gets hot\n- 14:30: Scooter to the Maasin river rope swing (Scooter rental about PHP 500 per day)\n- 19:00: Dinner and live music in General Luna\n\n**Day 3: Island hopping: Naked, Daku, Guyam**\n- 08:00: Boat from the General Luna port (Shared tour about PHP 1,500 per person with lunch)\n- 08:30: Naked Island sandbar\n- 11:00: Daku Island, grilled seafood lunch\n- 14:00: Swim and snorkel at Guyam Island\n- 16:00: Back in town, free evening\n\n**Day 4: Sugba Lagoon, then fly home**\n- 06:30: Van to Del Carmen (Leave bags in the van or at the port)\n- 07:30: Boat to Sugba Lagoon, paddle board and swim (About PHP 1,200 per person for boat share and fees)\n- 12:00: Lunch in Del Carmen\n- 13:30: Sayak Airport, 10 min away (Afternoon flight out)\n\n**Estimated cost per person (sample prices)**\n- Return flight from Manila: PHP 7,500\n- Stay, 3 nights (half of a PHP 5,000 room): PHP 7,500\n- Airport vans, both ways: PHP 700\n- Surf lesson: PHP 1,500\n- Island hopping tour: PHP 1,500\n- Sugba Lagoon boat share and fees: PHP 1,200\n- Scooter rental, 2 days: PHP 1,000\n- Food and drinks, 4 days: PHP 4,000\n- **Estimated total: PHP 24,900**\n\n**Local tip:** bring cash. ATMs in General Luna often run dry on weekends and many small places take cash only. Walk the Cloud 9 boardwalk at sunrise, before the crowds and the heat.\n\nWant me to book this plan, make it cheaper, or add another surf day?",
